{{!--
  Page hero (GH-9): breadcrumbs, title, excerpt, tags and actions above every
  content page — see Figma node 3615:59150 (in the page), 2735:65619 (hero
  alone, light) and 2735:65779 (hero alone, dark). Every colour below is a
  design-system token (`.dt-text`, `.dt-breadcrumb-item`, `.dt-label`,
  `.dt-button`), so nothing here is theme-specific — dark mode falls out of
  dt-tokens.css's own `.dt-theme-dark` block for free.

  Renders on every default-layout page except when `:page-role: -hero` is
  set — see main.hbs, which decides once and passes the result down, and
  the existing `-toc` role (toc.css, 02-on-this-page.ts) for the same
  convention applied to a different part of the chrome. A page that opts
  out gets its <h1> back in the article instead (article.hbs).

  Authoring surface — every attribute below is optional, page.title is not:

    :description: A sentence or two.        hero excerpt AND <meta name="description">
    :page-tags: Beta, Internal               comma-separated, one .dt-label--grey each
    :page-action: Get started                primary button label
    :page-action-url: getting-started.adoc   its target — a page reference or a literal URL
    :page-action-secondary: View source       secondary (outlined) button
    :page-action-secondary-url: https://…

  An action renders only when BOTH its label and url attributes are set — a
  button that goes nowhere is worse than no button. `*-url` values are
  resolved through Antora's own `resolvePageURL` helper (registered globally
  by @antora/page-composer, mirrored by the preview harness — see gulp.d/
  tasks/build-preview-pages.js) when they resolve to a real page, and used
  as a literal URL otherwise — it returns undefined rather than throwing for
  something that isn't a page reference, so `(or (resolvePageURL …) …)` is
  enough, no custom helper needed.

  Order is primary action first, secondary second: this bundle's own call,
  not Figma's — the frames (2735:65700/65725) draw the outlined secondary
  button to the LEFT of the filled primary one; here DOM and visual order
  both put the primary action first.

  The right-hand slot carries the ToC toggle (GH-10): a
  `.dt-button--ghost .dt-button--icon-only` with `panel-left`
  (Figma frame 3615:59159), `hidden` until src/js/02-on-this-page.ts decides
  there is a ToC to control — same reasoning as theme-toggle.hbs and the
  side-menu toggle, a control with no handler must not render. Hidden
  outright below breakpoint m (hero.css / header.css's own per-breakpoint
  hiding of the version tag and search input is the precedent) — the ToC
  sits above the article there instead of beside it, with nothing to toggle.

  Tags render `.dt-label--grey`, not the `--white` variant Figma's mock
  shows: `--white`'s background is literally `--dt-color-bg-default`, i.e.
  the page background itself, so on this page (bg-default surface) it never
  paints a visible pill in EITHER theme — grey's `--dt-color-bg-low` against
  `--dt-color-content-default` is the only variant that actually contrasts
  against the page in both light and dark.

  The hero's left column (`.hero__main`) is capped at `--content-max-width`
  (780px, vars.css) — the same measure the article below shares (doc.css,
  GH-10) — while `.hero__row` itself spans the grid's full width so the
  ToC toggle above sits flush in the gutter rather than at the text
  measure's edge (Figma frame 3615:59159).
--}}
<div class="hero">
  <div class="dt-grid-layout dt-grid-layout--with-margin hero__grid">
    <div class="dt-grid-layout__item dt-grid-layout__item--span-full hero__row">
      <div class="hero__main">
{{> breadcrumbs}}
        <h1 class="hero__title dt-text dt-text--title-xl">{{{page.title}}}</h1>
{{#with page.description}}
        <p class="hero__excerpt dt-text dt-text--body-l">{{this}}</p>
{{/with}}
{{#with (split page.attributes.tags ',')}}
        <div class="hero__tags">
        {{#each this}}
          <div class="dt-label dt-label--grey">
            <span class="dt-label__content">{{this}}</span>
          </div>
        {{/each}}
        </div>
        {{/with}}
{{#if (and page.attributes.action page.attributes.[action-url])}}
        <div class="hero__actions">
          <a class="dt-button dt-button--primary dt-button--icon-and-label" href="{{{relativize (or (resolvePageURL page.attributes.[action-url]) page.attributes.[action-url])}}}">
            <span class="dt-button__content">{{page.attributes.action}}</span>
          </a>
        {{#if (and page.attributes.[action-secondary] page.attributes.[action-secondary-url])}}
          <a class="dt-button dt-button--secondary dt-button--icon-and-label" href="{{{relativize (or (resolvePageURL page.attributes.[action-secondary-url]) page.attributes.[action-secondary-url])}}}">
            <span class="dt-button__content">{{page.attributes.[action-secondary]}}</span>
          </a>
        {{/if}}
        </div>
{{/if}}
      </div>
      <div class="hero__aside">
        <button class="dt-button dt-button--ghost dt-button--icon-only toc-toggle" type="button" aria-controls="on-this-page" aria-expanded="true" hidden>
          <span class="dt-button__content">
            <span class="dt-button__icon dt-button__icon-icon">{{icon "panel-left"}}</span>
          </span>
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
